    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0656" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1333: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-11T23:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                                1928—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 11—1:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>453. Legation’s 1427, March 9th.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d536-f1"/> In the absence
                    of anyone in the Peking Foreign Office having the authority to handle and
                    account for the May installment of the portion of the 1901 indemnity remitted in
                        1908,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d536-f2"/> I am holding the Customs check for
                    this fund received by me today, pending the indications of some Chinese
                    governmental organ to transact these matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
